<!-- The launch on Android 12+'s splash screen (kb PHN-631, PHN-632): the system draws and plays this from its first
     frame, while the app's process is still starting; the app's launch (:design LaunchHost.kt) continues from the
     moment the splash says it reached. It is launch_mark (the f on its tile) at the launch's size, 112 dp, with
     FerbMark's amber dot and a halo like its blur (units: the mark's 96-unit tile). The system draws this icon in a
     box of about 280 dp, not the 288 its guidance names: measured on the emulator (Android 16, 420 dpi), the tile
     came out 2.7 % small, so the viewport is sized for that box.
     The motion is motion.json `launch` (Launch.kt): the whole mark, its dot in place, from the first frame (owner kb
     PHN-700: no drop, no hop, no give of the f), and from 900 ms the dot breathes to 0.86 and 0.72 opacity and back
     every 1800 ms (accelerate_decelerate is (1 - cos pi u) / 2). -->
